--- reading it --------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. FR-009's first condition holds on the board. The refusal names the pending state and both
   slots, happens after the signature check and the mount and before "Marking target slot ...
   bad", so nothing was written: the second attempt has no "Marking" and no "Updating" line, and
   `rauc status` afterwards is the one from before it (Activated rootfs.1 (B), both good).
2. The handler costs about one second of an install, and it does not get in the way when
   nothing is pending (install 1).
3. The update changed the device's own configuration and its install logic over the air: the
   handler arrived inside a bundle, and was in force from the first boot of the slot that
   carried it. That was the point of the whole mechanism, shown on something other than the
   version string.
4. SC-006 on the board: /data/keep, written before the first install, still reads "marker"
   after two installs and two reboots, and /data/rauc.status now exists (the "Failed to load
   system status" line is gone from rauc status).
5. The message is printed twice (RAUC's "Error: ..." from the protocol line and the "# ..."
   echo). Cosmetic, left as it is: a change would need another over-the-air update to show.
6. Not shown on hardware: the second condition (two installs at once; host-checked only), and
   `fw_printenv` after the refusal.
